{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfeF4f3DSLrxjQvLL2gb9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is coherently structured, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- **New `Soundex` class is well-placed.** Extracting the algorithm into its own package-private class, shared by both `OwnerIdentity` (key segment) and `PossibleDuplicate` (surname match), puts the logic in the right unit and avoids duplicating it across the two consumers. Its javadoc documents the algorithm and both call sites.\n\n- **`OwnerIdentity` stays cohesive.** The two-level `key(normalized parts)` → `of(raw parts)` → `of(Owner)` layering mirrors the original design (pure builder vs. normalize-then-build), and the private `sha256hex` helper is a natural fit for a class whose single job is deriving the identity key. It hasn't become a catch-all.\n\n- **Dead code is properly removed.** `Household.hasMember` was only used by the duplicate gate and the soft-match rule, both of which no longer need it, so its removal is correct cleanup — no orphaned helper is left behind. `Household` retains only `size`/`maxMemberLevel`, which remain genuinely used.\n\n- **Responsibilities land where they belong.** `ValidateUniqueIdentity` is now the single identity-key gate (no longer taking `@Val Household.Id`), `ResolveHousehold`/`BuildOwner` keep the household id purely for the size/level rules, and `PossibleDuplicate` owns the soft-match semantics. The split reads naturally.\n\n- **Documentation hygiene is thorough.** Every touched class javadoc, the YAML step comments, the escalation exception doc, and the OpenAPI descriptions were all updated consistently to reflect the single-identity-key design, with cross-`@link`s kept accurate (e.g. the `PossibleDuplicate`/`OwnerIdentity`/`ValidateUniqueIdentity` references).\n\nMinor, non-blocking observations (not worth a change on their own): the manual `String.format(\"%02x\", …)` hex loop could be `HexFormat.of().formatHex(...)`, and the \"scan `ActiveOwners` comparing `OwnerIdentity.of(existing)`\" shape recurs in both `ValidateUniqueIdentity` and `PossibleDuplicate` — but their semantics differ (throw-on-match vs. skip-match-while-seeking-soft-match), so inlining each is the reasonable call rather than forcing a shared helper."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20885,"cache_read_input_tokens":11894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20885},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bf66f89-714e-46c4-9474-7219570a0038","uuid":"88e2229a-c81a-45f8-85ee-9c5f8af799eb","timestamp":"2026-10-02T23:02:38.393Z","request_id":"req_011CfeF4ejbzufNEkJKUMw6N"}
